cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you reuse this vocabulary, or cite metadata annotated with it,
  please cite the repository as below.
title: "IWAC Vocabulary"
version: "1.5"
date-released: 2026-10-19
abstract: >-
  An RDF vocabulary for recording AI processing provenance and multi-model
  sentiment annotation in a digital archive. It defines value-annotation
  properties naming the model behind an OCR pass, summary, transcription,
  named-entity run or authority description, and a model-keyed property set
  that stores the centrality, polarity and subjectivity readings of a panel
  of large language models side by side rather than collapsing them into one
  score. Built for the Islam
  West Africa Collection (IWAC) on Omeka S, and reusable by any collection that
  needs to say which model produced which value.
type: dataset
keywords:
  - RDF vocabulary
  - ontology
  - Omeka S
  - digital humanities
  - Islam West Africa
  - large language models
  - sentiment analysis
  - provenance
  - digital archives
  - African studies
